  "finding": "4 of 12 ladder rungs are admissible for ALL 8 traits simultaneously: [1.0, 2.0, 5.0, 10.0]. A rung admissible on the full 1,135-accession panel can be INADMISSIBLE for a trait whose missingness concentrates one cluster above the one-fold share, so rung admissibility is a per-trait property and selecting it on the genotype set alone over-states the usable range.",
  "honest_limits": [
    "This is a STRUCTURAL census: no model is fitted, so it says which rungs COULD be used, never which would show a de-confounding response.",
    "Clustering is greedy-representative (chaining-resistant) on this repo's IBS over a MAF->=0.05 marker subsample -- not an LD-pruned genome-wide distance.",
    "The bar is 1/n_splits, so it moves with n_splits; it is a validity constraint on grouped CV, not a tunable threshold.",
    "Admissibility is evaluated on each trait's non-missing subset, which is the set grouped CV actually folds."
  ]
